Jamie (SG Eco Loop): then you have now gone so wide that, oh, there are too many things for you to do, right? That, you know, there are so many problems in the world, what are you gonna do? Is you now need to kind of choose. So you need to choose the right problem to solve. So maybe you do a survey, 10 people tell you, I have this problem, and then one person tells you, I have this other problem.

391
01:09:40.859 --> 01:09:44.480
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): Would you solve the problem for the 10 people, or for the 1 person?

392
01:09:44.569 --> 01:10:02.610
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): So you will choose the… you will probably choose the problem that exists for more people, or you choose the problem that is bigger. You don't choose a problem that, you know, only, like, two people have. You choose a problem that's like, oh, it's actually faced by millions of people, or, you know, everybody will face it on a regular basis. You choose problems that are meaningful.

393
01:10:03.550 --> 01:10:08.880
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): And then… When you are very clear what is the problem you want to tackle.

394
01:10:09.730 --> 01:10:13.559
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): Some important questions would be to say, what is the problem?

395
01:10:13.850 --> 01:10:28.610
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): who faces this problem? So, if you are very generic and very vague, then that's not a good sign, because when… before you move into solution, if you cannot be very clear who you are targeting, what is the problem you are targeting.

396
01:10:28.740 --> 01:10:40.530
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): You know, that's your foundation, right? That means your foundation's not strong, then whatever you put on top, maybe it's totally wrong. So you need to know what are the challenges, what is the context, that we have, okay?

397
01:10:41.700 --> 01:10:42.630
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): So…

398
01:10:43.310 --> 01:10:52.879
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): First diamond is more on the problem. Second diamond, so we are starting to go into the second diamond, which is the solution. So when you are first starting to think about solutions for a problem.

399
01:10:53.980 --> 01:10:55.959
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): Focus on being creative.

400
01:10:56.210 --> 01:10:57.780
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): Think outside the box.

401
01:10:59.090 --> 01:11:02.459
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): Come up with anything and everything, write them all down.

402
01:11:02.590 --> 01:11:09.229
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): sometimes at the back of your head, you'll be like, yeah, this one is not possible, this one's not feasible, this one's too difficult. You have all of these things in your head.

403
01:11:09.370 --> 01:11:13.870
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): When you're ideating, that's not the right time to think about the limitations.

404
01:11:14.430 --> 01:11:17.489
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): Put aside the limitations, and just be creative.

405
01:11:17.700 --> 01:11:34.479
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): right now. You can also research, you know, what other people are doing, you can sometimes see, maybe some solutions that are in a different industry, maybe not in sustainability, that they have done that's very interesting. Can I apply to, this problem that I'm trying to solve? So be creative.

406
01:11:34.900 --> 01:11:43.809
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): Then, you have now also gone very wide, and you had to choose what you actually build. Because you cannot build all of this. You have, like, 10 ideas, doesn't mean you can build a prototype for 10 ideas, too many.

407
01:11:43.980 --> 01:11:50.349
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): So, prioritizing. So that's when you put in a little bit more thinking into, okay, for this idea.

408
01:11:51.400 --> 01:11:53.020
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): How will I implement it?

409
01:11:53.470 --> 01:11:55.210
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): Is it feasible at all?

410
01:11:56.270 --> 01:12:11.109
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): Can it scale? And can it give me a big impact? Can I say, oh, like, maybe this idea can only help me divert 10 kg of waste a year? That's very, very little. Versus this other idea that I think can divert away 100KG of waste a year.

411
01:12:11.180 --> 01:12:17.390
Jamie (SG Eco Loop): That's a lot more, right, than the other one. So then you can use that to, prioritize

